## Details

Reads a Docker install's `status --json --values` without managing it, by the installer it keeps
(`<work_dir>/<name>/<short_name>-stow status --json --values`, through the same scripts as the
resource's read), on a host reached over SSH or on the machine running OpenTofu. Nothing on the
target changes, and no installer image is fetched. The read is bounded by 5 minutes. No install in
the directory (`No install`) and another project's (`Another project's install`) are errors.

| Argument | | |
|---|---|---|
| `name`, `short_name` | required | The project's name (the install directory `<name>/`; compared with the status's) and the installer's short name, one path element each. |
| `host`, `port`, `user`, `private_key_file`, `known_hosts_line`, `work_dir` | optional | As `stowage_docker_install`'s (left out, `host` is this machine and `work_dir` the home; `work_dir` an absolute, clean path). |

| Attribute | |
|---|---|
| `id` | `<work_dir>/<name>`. |
| `installed`, `previous` | `{version, revision, installer}`; null before the first install, and when the install keeps no release for `rollback`. |
| `channel`, `status` | As the resource's. |
| `inputs` | The input keys the install records, sorted, never a value; null when the installer does not tell. |
| `registry`, `registry_ca_digest`, `address` | What the first install recorded; null when the status gives none. |
| `pull_login` | Whether the install holds its own registry login (`status --json --values` `pull_login`); null from an installer that does not tell (before Stowage 0.40.0). |
